From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: arm64: dts: h713: add the L018 board dts

The L018 (stock Android 11 of 2025-05-14, Projector05141211) has the
HY310's DRAM words, panel (project 0x30) and display firmware, so its tree
is the HY310's with what this board's own stock device tree and its pin
state under stock (read on a running unit, 24.10.2026) say differently:

- motor_ctr off: PH4/PH5 are twi2 here, the accelerometer's bus, and
  PH6/PH7 are on function 2; the HY310's focus motor drives PH4..PH7 and
  homes at probe. This board's own motor is on PF0..PF3 and is not
  described yet.
- twi1 off: PH2/PH3 are disabled under stock.
- The fan tacho is PH13, as on the HY200 QZ713DF A1. PH17 carries the fan's
  PWM0 (95/70/60 % with the lamp at high/std/low under stock); U-Boot's
  CONFIG_H713_BOARD_L018 sets the stock std 70 %, and this tree leaves
  PH17 and PWM0 as they are found.
- The lamp is PWM2 on PB4 (function 2 under stock, 25 kHz) and dims as the
  duty rises: the three stock modes, switched on the running unit, are
  high 30 %, std 50 %, low 75 %. The dtsi's pwm-backlight stays with
  brightness-levels <100 75 50 30> (pwm-backlight scales by the largest
  level), so brightness 75 is stock high and the brightest it drives, 50
  stock std and the start.
- The NTC: the L018 has one (stock ntc_num 1, GPADC channel 1), the HY310
  none; its own gpadc-table (0..55 C) and thresholds (warn 41, power off
  51, resume 34 C), verbatim from the stock tree.
- The vendor ARISC firmware, as on the HY300 Pro.

Nothing of it has booted on the board yet.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy310.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-l018.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-h728-x96qpro+.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-t527-avaota-a1.dtb
diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-l018.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-l018.dts
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-l018.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,106 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+/*
+ * L018 projector (Allwinner H713; stock Android 11 of 2025-05-14,
+ * Projector05141211).
+ *
+ * The HY310's tree, held against this board's own stock device tree (the
+ * kernel's in vendor_boot and U-Boot's in the sunxi package are the same
+ * here) and against its pin state under stock (24.10.2026). The DRAM words,
+ * the panel (project 0x30) and the display firmware are the HY310's. What
+ * differs, and what this file does about it:
+ *
+ *  - PH4/PH5 are twi2 on this board, the bus of its accelerometer (lsm6dsv
+ *    at 0x6a), and PH6/PH7 are on function 2. The HY310's focus motor drives
+ *    PH4..PH7 and homes at probe, so motor_ctr is off. This board's own motor
+ *    (phases PF0..PF3, end switch PB1) is not described yet.
+ *  - twi1 (PH2/PH3, the HY310's SC7A20) is disabled under stock: off here.
+ *  - The fan: the tacho is PH13 (stock fan0 fg-gpio, on EINT under stock) -
+ *    the board manager powers off when it counts too little, so it has to
+ *    count the right pin. Its speed is PWM0 on PH17 (function 3 under stock:
+ *    95/70/60 % with the lamp at high/std/low). U-Boot (CONFIG_H713_BOARD_L018)
+ *    sets PWM0 to the stock std 70 % before the fan's rail comes up, and this
+ *    tree leaves PH17 and PWM0 as they are found.
+ *  - The lamp: PWM2 on PB4 (function 2 = pwm2 under stock, 25 kHz), and it
+ *    dims as the duty rises - the three stock modes, switched on a running
+ *    unit with the registers read along (24.10.2026): high 30 %, std 50 %,
+ *    low 75 %, the fan's PWM0 at 95/70/60 %. The dtsi's pwm-backlight keeps
+ *    its PWM with exactly those duties (below).
+ *  - PB5 enables lamp and fan as on the HY310 (stock fan0 fan-power-gpio,
+ *    output high under stock); the board manager keeps it.
+ *  - The vendor ARISC firmware, as on the HY300 Pro: crust has run on the
+ *    HY310 only.
+ *
+ * Not described yet: the accelerometer, the focus motor, the LEDs (PL0/PL1).
+ * The camera is USB and needs nothing here. The board has no keys but the
+ * power key (PL4, as on the HY310); the stock tree's seven LRADC keys are its
+ * template.
+ */
+
+#include "sun50i-h713-hy310.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "L018 (Allwinner H713)";
+	compatible = "magcubic,l018", "allwinner,sun50i-h713";
+};
+
+&twi1 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&motor_ctr {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&board_mgr {
+	/*
+	 * The L018 has an NTC (stock ntc_num = 1; ntc0: source 1 = GPADC,
+	 * channel 1 - the dtsi's ntc0 says the same), the HY310 none (stock
+	 * ntc_num = 0). Its own table and thresholds, verbatim from its stock
+	 * tree: 38 pairs <degrees C, mV> from 0 to 55 C (the HY310's runs to
+	 * 80 C), warn 41, power off 51, resume 34 C. The stock vmlinux of both
+	 * boards converts with the same code (get_adc_data, get_temp_data,
+	 * search_table_gpadc, sunxi_gpadc_read_*: the same sizes). Below the
+	 * last node both clamp to 55 C, which is above temp_poweroff, so a
+	 * hotter box still counts towards the shutdown. temp_resume is read by
+	 * the stock driver only (it ends its thermal mode 3 there).
+	 */
+	io-channels = <&gpadc 1>;
+	gpadc-table = <
+		0x0 0x5E6 0x5 0x5B4 0x14 0x4F8 0x15 0x4EA 0x16 0x4DC 0x17 0x4CD
+		0x18 0x4BF 0x19 0x4B0 0x1A 0x4A1 0x1B 0x492 0x1C 0x483 0x1D 0x474
+		0x1E 0x464 0x1F 0x455 0x20 0x446 0x21 0x437 0x22 0x427 0x23 0x418
+		0x24 0x408 0x25 0x3F9 0x26 0x3E9 0x27 0x3D9 0x28 0x3CA 0x29 0x3BA
+		0x2A 0x3AB 0x2B 0x39B 0x2C 0x38C 0x2D 0x37D 0x2E 0x36D 0x2F 0x35E
+		0x30 0x34F 0x31 0x340 0x32 0x331 0x33 0x323 0x34 0x314 0x35 0x306
+		0x36 0x2F8 0x37 0x2E9>;
+	temp_warn = <41>;
+	temp_poweroff = <51>;
+	temp_resume = <34>;
+
+	fan0 {
+		fg-gpio = <&pio 7 13 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;	/* PH13, stock fan0 fg-gpio */
+	};
+
+	ntc {
+		ntc_num = <1>;
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * pwm-backlight scales by the largest level, so the duties have to be the
+ * levels themselves with 100 among them, and as the lamp dims with the duty
+ * they run downwards: brightness 0..75 goes from 100 % (darker than stock low)
+ * to 30 % (stock high, the brightest the stock firmware drives); 25 is stock
+ * low, 50 stock std and the start. Brightness 0 itself switches the PWM off
+ * (the driver clears the channel's enable and clock gate); what the pin and
+ * the lamp then do is not measured, and nothing of ours writes 0.
+ */
+&backlight {
+	brightness-levels = <100 75 50 30>;
+	num-interpolated-steps = <25>;
+	default-brightness-level = <50>;	/* 50 %, stock std */
+};
+
+&arisc {
+	firmware-name = "h713-arisc.bin", "hy310-edid.bin";
+};
